                <pb facs="0483" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg473"/>

                <head>Appendix 242</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Shipments From German Austria to
                        Serbia</hi></p>
                <p>Following telegram sent to Mr. Hoover by Captain Gregory, Chief of the American
                    Mission, at Vienna.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p rendition="#right">“Vienna, July 14, 1919.</p>
                    <p rendition="#flush">Hoover <lb/> Paris.</p>
                    <p>Italian military mission here is insisting on necessity of specific
                        permission granted by it for each shipment steel and bridge materials
                        shipped by Austrians to Serb Kingdom. This material shipped as compensation
                        for foodstuffs and delays occasioned by Italian attitude are irritating
                        Serbs who though [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] cut off food shipments
                        from Banat. Will you please have a resolution passed at next meeting <pb
                            facs="0484" n="474" xml:id="pg474"/> Supreme Economic Council covering
                        these shipments in block as Italian Mission here claims to act in this
                        matter under authority Supreme Economic Council.</p>
                    <p rendition="#right">Gregory”</p></quote>
            </div>
